From 05ae8f484bd0b32d8f0bded0ac5bc721d0dcf972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:15:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 0028: the report reaches the stick with no mount

A 0027 report needs /Volumes/OPENCORE to exist, and this machine has boots where macOS
never mounts the stick, so nothing comes back. The same report now also goes into the
pre-created NAVI48.TXT through the block device: find the IOMedia in the stick's size
class, accept it only if sector 0 is a FAT32 BPB labelled OPENCORE, the root directory
holds the exact 8.3 entry NAVI48.TXT, and the file starts with "navi"; then rewrite the
fixed 1536-byte text region of its first cluster. FAT, directory and other clusters are
never written. The VFS path is tried first and keeps working when the volume mounts; the
raw path runs only when it does not. Same fixed length on both, no truncation, so the
Windows-created 8 KiB target keeps its shape. Host suite and a mutation harness cover the
BPB parser, the directory scan and the write-safety predicate.
---
